# 11. Real-world example — Shared development folder

Imagine a development team:

```text
developers
```

has access to:

```text
/company/project
```

We want all files created there to belong to the `developers` group.

We can configure:

```bash
chmod 2775 /company/project
```

Now:

```text
/company/project
        │
        ├── app.py
        ├── database.py
        ├── config.txt
        └── README.md
```

New files inherit the directory's group.

This makes collaboration much easier.

